# Slice C guard fixture: a lone legacy `main/0` is run by the entry selector after the top-level statements.
# Expected: `top`, then `main0`, then the entry result 10.
# Inline documentation keeps this guard within the bounded C++ host syntax.
main() = "Legacy zero-argument entry point that prints `main0` and returns 10." { print("main0"); 10 }
print("top")
42
